\section{Discussion}
\label{sec:discussion}

\paragraph{Type--mechanism dissociation and intervention design.}
The type--mechanism dissociation ($V = 0.45$ vs.\ $0.14$) reframes the taxonomy as a diagnostic instrument; prompt-based mitigation is type-dependent (Appendix~\ref{app:mitigation}). The 60.8\% residual variance reflects clause-level interactions (Appendix~\ref{app:residual}), motivating clause-level auditing over type-level screening. These findings identify causal mechanisms, not deployment-ready effect sizes; SOPBench ($+$12.7\,pp; Appendix~\ref{app:sopbench}) confirms directional consistency.

